[% INCLUDE 'doc-head-open.inc' %]
<title>RFID desk &rsaquo; Plugins &rsaquo; Koha</title>
[% INCLUDE 'doc-head-close.inc' %]
</head>
<body id="plugins_rfiddesk_configure" class="plugins">
[% INCLUDE 'header.inc' %]
[% INCLUDE 'cat-search.inc' %]

<nav id="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb">
    <ol>
        <li><a href="/cgi-bin/koha/mainpage.pl">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/cgi-bin/koha/plugins/plugins-home.pl">Plugins</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" aria-current="page">RFID desk &rsaquo; Configuration</a></li>
    </ol>
</nav>

<div class="main container-fluid">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
            <h1>RFID desk: configuration</h1>
            <p>Each circulation desk PC runs the <strong>koha-rfid desk agent</strong>, which owns the
               RFID reader and label printer. The staff interface talks to it on the PC itself.</p>

            <form method="get" class="form-horizontal">
                <input type="hidden" name="class" value="[% CLASS | html %]" />
                <input type="hidden" name="method" value="[% METHOD | html %]" />
                <input type="hidden" name="save" value="1" />

                <fieldset class="rows">
                    <ol>
                        <li>
                            <label for="agent_url">Desk agent address:</label>
                            <input type="text" id="agent_url" name="agent_url" size="40" value="[% agent_url | html %]" />
                            <div class="hint">Normally <code>http://127.0.0.1:8765</code>. Must match <code>listen_port</code> in the agent's agent.ini.
                                The agent must also list this staff interface's address in <code>allowed_origins</code>.</div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <label for="enable_checkout">Check out page:</label>
                            <input type="checkbox" id="enable_checkout" name="enable_checkout" value="1" [% IF enable_checkout %]checked="checked"[% END %] />
                            <span class="hint">Show the RFID pad panel and "Check out N books".</span>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <label for="enable_checkin">Check in page:</label>
                            <input type="checkbox" id="enable_checkin" name="enable_checkin" value="1" [% IF enable_checkin %]checked="checked"[% END %] />
                            <span class="hint">Show the RFID pad panel and "Check in N books".</span>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <label for="enable_labels">RFID labels:</label>
                            <input type="checkbox" id="enable_labels" name="enable_labels" value="1" [% IF enable_labels %]checked="checked"[% END %] />
                            <span class="hint">"RFID labels" button on bibliographic records (needs a label printer set in the agent).</span>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </fieldset>
                <fieldset class="action">
                    <input type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" value="Save" />
                    <a class="cancel" href="/cgi-bin/koha/plugins/plugins-home.pl">Cancel</a>
                </fieldset>
            </form>

            <h2 id="desk-setup">Set up a desk PC</h2>
            [% IF agent_files.size %]
            <p>On the desk PC, open this page, then open <strong>PowerShell as administrator</strong>
               (Start menu, type <em>PowerShell</em>, right-click, <em>Run as administrator</em>), paste this command and press Enter:</p>
            <pre id="rfid-setup-command" style="white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all;"></pre>
            <p><button type="button" class="btn btn-default" id="rfid-setup-copy">Copy command</button>
               <span id="rfid-setup-copied" class="hint" style="display: none;">Copied.</span></p>
            <ul>
                <li>It installs the desk agent [% plugin_version | html %] (and Python 3.12 if needed), and starts it in the background from then on.
                    The PC needs internet access during the install, for the Python packages.</li>
                <li>The first time, it asks for the RFID reader's IP address, the pad power and the label printer's IP address. Press Enter to skip any of them.
                    They are kept in <code>C:\koha-rfid\agent.ini</code>.</li>
                <li>After upgrading this plugin, update each desk PC with <code>C:\koha-rfid\install_agent.ps1 -Update</code> (as administrator),
                    or paste the command again.</li>
                <li>Check a desk with <code>C:\koha-rfid\install_agent.ps1 -Status</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="hint">Files, if you need them by hand:
                [% FOREACH f IN agent_files %]<a href="[% static_base | html %]/[% f | uri %]">[% f | html %]</a>[% UNLESS loop.last %] &middot; [% END %][% END %]
            </p>
            <script>
            (function () {
                // $k is the staff address exactly as this browser sees it: the agent
                // only answers pages from that address (allowed_origins).
                var cmd = "[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol='Tls12'; $k='" + location.origin + "'; "
                        + "iwr -UseBasicParsing \"$k[% static_base | html %]/install_agent.ps1\" -OutFile \"$env:TEMP\\install_agent.ps1\"; "
                        + "powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"$env:TEMP\\install_agent.ps1\" -Koha $k";
                var pre = document.getElementById("rfid-setup-command");
                pre.textContent = cmd;
                document.getElementById("rfid-setup-copy").addEventListener("click", function () {
                    var done = function () { document.getElementById("rfid-setup-copied").style.display = "inline"; };
                    if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
                        navigator.clipboard.writeText(cmd).then(done);
                    } else {   // plain http: select the text and copy it the old way
                        var range = document.createRange();
                        range.selectNodeContents(pre);
                        var sel = window.getSelection();
                        sel.removeAllRanges();
                        sel.addRange(range);
                        if (document.execCommand("copy")) { done(); }
                    }
                });
            })();
            </script>
            [% ELSE %]
            <div class="dialog alert">This copy of the plugin doesn't carry the desk agent. Build the plugin with
                <code>python deploy/build_plugin.py</code> and upload that <code>.kpz</code>, then restart plack.</div>
            [% END %]
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

[% INCLUDE 'intranet-bottom.inc' %]
